/*
H2_LEVEL.C

A Halo 2 level made into a cache file of this engine's (h2_level.h).

What a Halo 2 structure BSP holds and how it is read (the layouts checked
against the owner's 01a_tutorial.map; the cache itself: h2_cache.c):
- its tag (0x23C bytes): collision materials at 0x0C (0x14 each: old
  shader reference, then the shader at 0x0C), the collision BSP at 0x14,
  vehicle floor and ceiling at 0x1C/0x20, leaves at 0x2C (8 bytes: cluster,
  surface reference count, first), world bounds at 0x34, cluster portals at
  0x5C (0x24 each: back and front cluster, plane, centroid, radius, flags,
  vertices), clusters at 0x9C (0xB0 each), materials at 0xA4 (0x20 each:
  old shader at 0, shader at 8), instanced geometry definitions at 0x138
  (0xC8 each) and instances at 0x140 (0x58 each: scale, forward, left, up,
  position, definition index at 0x34);
- a cluster's or a definition's render geometry: a resource block (its
  file reference at 0x28, size 0x2C, section size 0x30, resources at 0x38:
  type, locators, element size or buffer index, size, offset): 'blkh' and a
  size, the section (parts at +0, strip indices at +0x20, vertex buffers'
  descriptors at +0x38 - a type and a stride each), then the resources'
  data; parts are 0x48 bytes (type, flags, material, index start and count:
  triangle lists, counter-clockwise), vertex buffer type 0x01 positions
  (3 floats), 0x18 texture coordinates (2 floats), 0x1B normal, binormal
  and tangent (three 11:11:10 words, the Xbox's packing and this engine's
  own), 0x1F lightmap coordinates (two signed 16-bit fractions);
- a collision BSP (0x40 bytes: eight blocks): 3D nodes of 8 bytes (a plane,
  then the back and front children as 24-bit indices, a leaf's with the top
  bit, 0xFFFFFF none - halo2-decomp src/collision.c h2_collision_leaf),
  planes, leaves of 4 bytes, 2D references and nodes, surfaces of 8 bytes,
  edges of 12, vertices of 16: this engine's, with 16-bit indices whose top
  bit is the flag this engine keeps in its 32-bit indices' top bit;
- the lightmap tag: its group (0x80) has 256-colour palettes (0x08, 1 KB
  each, BGRA), its bitmap (0x18), each cluster's page and palette (0x28,
  4 bytes each) and each instance's (0x48); a page is P8, swizzled as the
  Xbox swizzles.
A lightmap texel's colour is its palette's entry, its channels in 0..1:
halo2-decomp src/bitmap.c h2_bitmap_lightmap_rgb (the retail XBE's scale
there is 1/255); the scale the environment shaders give it on top is the
lightmap scale below (HALO_H2_LIGHTMAP_SCALE, 4: lightmaps_begin).
*/

